iv> <div class=3D"md-content" data-md-component=3D"content"> <article class=
=3D"md-content__inner md-typeset"> <h1 id=3D"bar-events">Bar events</h1> <p=
>Algorithm developers often need to refer to bar events in order to execute=
 trading strategies on time in response to the updated prices. The API offe=
rs the <code class=3D"highlight"><span class=3D"n">BarOpened</span></code> =
and <code class=3D"highlight"><span class=3D"n">BarClosed</span></code> eve=
nts for algo creators to fine-tune cBots and grasp opportunities at differe=
nt points of the bar cycle. </p> <div class=3D"admonition note"> <p class=
=3D"admonition-title">Note</p> <p>Bar events can only be handled when codin=
g cBots. Indicators, instead, have the <code class=3D"highlight"><span clas=
s=3D"n">Calculate</span><span class=3D"p">()</span></code> method that is c=
alled on every tick.</p> </div> <p>In this guide, we explain the difference=
 between the <code class=3D"highlight"><span class=3D"n">OnBar</span><span =
class=3D"p">()</span></code> and <code class=3D"highlight"><span class=3D"n=
">OnBarClosed</span><span class=3D"p">()</span></code> methods and provide =
several use cases. </p> <div class=3D"admonition info"> <p class=3D"admonit=
ion-title">Bar events in one minute!</p> <ul> <li>The <code class=3D"highli=
ght"><span class=3D"n">OnBar</span><span class=3D"p">()</span></code> metho=
d is triggered every time a new bar is drawn on the chart to which an insta=
nce is added. It is called for the newly formed bar.</li> <li>The <code cla=
ss=3D"highlight"><span class=3D"n">OnBarClosed</span><span class=3D"p">()</=
span></code> event handler is also triggered on each new bar. However, it i=
s called for the last closed (that is, previous to the current) bar.</li> <=
li>Referring to the correct bar event, you increase the accuracy of your te=
chnical analysis and select appropriate timing for algorithm actions.</li> =
<li>The supported chart types for <code class=3D"highlight"><span class=3D"=
n">BarOpened</span></code> and <code class=3D"highlight"><span class=3D"n">=
BarClosed</span></code> are time bars, candlesticks, tick, Renko, range and=
 Heikin Ashi charts.</li> </ul> </div> <h2 id=3D"use-the-onbar-method">Use =
the <code>OnBar()</code> method</h2> <p>The occurrence of the <code class=
=3D"highlight"><span class=3D"n">BarOpened</span></code> event depends on a=
 symbol schedule and the frequency of coming prices. Usually, platform user=
s can adjust the occurrence of <code class=3D"highlight"><span class=3D"n">=
BarClosed</span></code> with the chart timeframe settings.</p> <div class=
=3D"admonition note"> <p class=3D"admonition-title">Note</p> <p>The <code c=
lass=3D"highlight"><span class=3D"n">OnBar</span><span class=3D"p">()</span=
></code> method can be called as frequently as the chart timeframe settings=
 allow. Once a bar closes, <code class=3D"highlight"><span class=3D"n">OnBa=
r</span><span class=3D"p">()</span></code> will not be triggered until the =
next tick arrives, which logically triggers a new bar to be formed. </p> </=
div> <p>The <code class=3D"highlight"><span class=3D"n">OnBar</span><span c=
lass=3D"p">()</span></code> method is invoked simultaneously with every new=
 bar drawn on the chart to which an algorithm is attached. As a result, the=
 <code class=3D"highlight"><span class=3D"n">OnBar</span><span class=3D"p">=
()</span></code> handler is the perfect place to define custom trading logi=
c that your cBot should repeat regularly.</p> <p>In the code editor, you ca=
n specify the <code class=3D"highlight"><span class=3D"n">OnBar</span><span=
 class=3D"p">()</span></code> handler as follows:</p> <div class=3D"highlig=
ht"><pre id=3D"__code_71"><span></span><nav class=3D"md-code__nav"><button =
class=3D"md-code__button" title=3D"Copy to clipboard" data-clipboard-target=
=3D"#__code_71 &gt; code" data-md-type=3D"copy"></button></nav><code>overri=
de void OnBar()
</code></pre></div> <h2 id=3D"use-the-onbarclosed-method">Use the <code>OnB=
arClosed()</code> method</h2> <p>The Algo API also allows for executing log=
ic for the last closed bar, which, depending on the strategy you want to im=
plement, may be a more convenient and accurate alternative to handling the =
<code class=3D"highlight"><span class=3D"n">BarOpened</span></code> event. =
On bar open, the new bar appears as a (doji candle) and does not contain co=
mplete data for technical analysis. </p> <p>The <code class=3D"highlight"><=
span class=3D"n">BarClosed</span></code> event is an alias of the <code cla=
ss=3D"highlight"><span class=3D"n">BarOpened</span></code> event, meaning t=
hat it occurs only in case the <code class=3D"highlight"><span class=3D"n">=
BarOpened</span></code> event happens. For example, the <code class=3D"high=
light"><span class=3D"n">BarClosed</span></code> event for the last bar on =
Friday will occur with the first opened bar on Monday, provided that the sy=
mbol is not traded over the weekend. </p> <div class=3D"admonition note"> <=
p class=3D"admonition-title">Note</p> <p>The <code class=3D"highlight"><spa=
n class=3D"n">OnBarClosed</span><span class=3D"p">()</span></code> method w=
ill not be called until a tick arrives to form the new bar.</p> </div> <p>T=
he <code class=3D"highlight"><span class=3D"n">OnBarClosed</span><span clas=
s=3D"p">()</span></code> event handler can be declared as follows:</p> <div=
 class=3D"highlight"><pre id=3D"__code_72"><span></span><nav class=3D"md-co=
de__nav"><button class=3D"md-code__button" title=3D"Copy to clipboard" data=
-clipboard-target=3D"#__code_72 &gt; code" data-md-type=3D"copy"></button><=
/nav><code>override void OnBarClosed()
</code></pre></div> <p>In the body of the <code class=3D"highlight"><span c=
lass=3D"n">OnBarClosed</span><span class=3D"p">()</span></code> method, you=
 can determine what connected actions your cBots will perform when the <cod=
e class=3D"highlight"><span class=3D"n">BarClosed</span></code> event is tr=
iggered (for example, execute an order, outline a pattern, draw technical a=
nalysis visuals, etc.). </p> <p>When accessed in this event handler, the <c=
ode>Bars</code> collection does not contain the current live bar, whereas o=
ther collections (such as, <code>Positions</code>, <code>Symbols</code>, et=
c.) contain actual data.</p> <p>The <code class=3D"highlight"><span class=
=3D"n">OnBar</span><span class=3D"p">()</span></code> and <code class=3D"hi=
ghlight"><span class=3D"n">OnBarClosed</span><span class=3D"p">()</span></c=
ode> event handlers work as intended in backtesting and optimisation. Both =
methods can be used on different chart types, including time bars, candlest=
icks, tick, Renko, range and Heikin Ashi charts.</p> <h2 id=3D"create-examp=
le-cbots">Create example cBots</h2> <p>The following example cBot places a =
market order when every third bar on the EURCHF chart is opened. </p> <div =
